hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20908","Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated to us from Abd Rabbihi al-Hujaymi from Jabir ibn Sulaym or Sulaym who said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he was sitting with his companions. He said: I said: Which of you is the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: Either he gestured to himself or the people pointed to him. He said: He was sitting leaning on a cloak whose fringe had fallen upon his feet. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am distant from some things, so teach me. He said: Fear Allah, mighty and majestic, and do not belittle any good deed, even pouring from your bucket into the vessel of one seeking water, and beware of pride, for Allah, blessed and exalted, does not love pride, and if a man reviles you and reproaches you for something he knows in you, do not reproach him for something you know in him, so its reward will be for you and its sin upon him, and do not revile anyone."
"20909","Yazid narrated to us, Sallam ibn Miskin informed us from Aqil ibn Talhah, Abu Jurayy al-Hujaymi narrated to us, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are desert people, so teach us something by which Allah, blessed and exalted, will benefit us. He said: Do not belittle any good deed, even pouring from your bucket into the vessel of one seeking water, even speaking to your brother with your face cheerful to him, and beware of letting the lower garment trail, for it is from arrogance, and arrogance Allah, mighty and majestic, does not love, and if a man reviles you for what he knows in you, do not revile him for what you know in him, for its reward is for you and its burden upon the one who said it."
"20910","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Sallam narrated to us, Aqil ibn Talhah narrated to us from Abu Jurayy al-Hujaymi that he came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, among people from the desert, and they said: We are desert people, then he mentioned the hadith, except that he said: So do not revile him for what you know in him, for the reward of that is for you and its burden upon him."
"20911","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, Ubaydah al-Hujaymi narrated to us from Abu Tamimah al-Hujaymi from Abu Jurayy Jabir ibn Sulaym who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was sitting leaning on a shawl of his whose fringe had fallen upon his feet, and I said: Which of you is Muhammad or the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he gestured with his hand to himself. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am from the desert people and in me is their roughness, so advise me. He said: Do not belittle any good deed, even meeting your brother with a cheerful face, even pouring from your bucket into the vessel of one seeking water, and if a man reviles you for what he knows in you, do not revile him for what you know in him, for its reward will be for you and its burden upon him, and beware of letting the lower garment trail, for letting the lower garment trail is from pride, and Allah, mighty and majestic, does not love pride, and do not revile anyone. So I never reviled anyone after him, neither sheep nor camel."
"20912","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us from Abu Tamimah al-Hujaymi from a man of Balhujaym who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, to what do you call. He said: I call to Allah alone, who if harm touches you and you call upon Him He removes it from you, and who if you stray in a barren land and you call upon Him He returns you, and who if a year of drought befalls you and you call upon Him He grows for you. He said: I said: So advise me. He said: Do not revile anyone, and do not refrain from any good deed, even meeting your brother with your face cheerful to him, even pouring from your bucket into the vessel of one seeking water, and wear the waist-wrapper to half the shin, and if you refuse then to the ankles, and beware of letting the lower garment trail, for letting the lower garment trail is from pride, and Allah, blessed and exalted, does not love pride."
